# NOTE: a bare `node_modules` matches ONLY the repository root — Docker matches
# each pattern against the whole context-relative path, so nested directories
# need the `**/` prefix. Without it, `COPY . .` drags the HOST's
# packages/*/node_modules into the image on top of the ones installed in the
# deps stage. pnpm's symlinks are absolute, so they dangle inside the container
# and the build dies with "Cannot find module .../typescript/bin/tsc".
# This only bites builds that upload a local working tree (docker build,
# fly deploy, railway up) — a git-clone build has no node_modules to leak.
.git
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/dist-worker
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/*.log
.env
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.local
